Interesting gender differences from my point of view would be:-

Food

Women can tell when food is off - they have a better sense of smell (this
is based on a limited experience of sharing mixed flats etc not a claim
as a scientific fact!).  

Men however do find it easier to open tins though in my experience they
do not know how to use tin openers!

Clothes

Many women do seem to be proud of their dress sense.  Perhaps the
occasional message "This feels right for you."  when looking at armour
could hint that it suited them - perhaps there could be some clothes
that would only fit women - stilleto shoes might be dangerous foot
weapons whilst reducing speed - a gown of Charisma that (if showing)
increases the characters charisma though leaves them rather
vulnerable...  Actually this clothes stuff should simply apply to those
with a slighter build whatever their sex - in otherwords I'm suggesting
clothes sizing (arg!).

Perhaps a makeup box to improve charisma (though I also suspect that
this might act as aggrevate monster too in the manner of warpaint...)
maybe this would work for both sexes - some men look really good in
makeup...

Women's clothes rarely have enough pockets on them - if wearing
specially designed women's clothes I think ones holding capactiy might
go down - though a handbag could be introduced (I used to play D&D, I
almost always role-played female characters and one of favourites was a
cleric who had a handbag with sufficient weight inside it to act as a
mace - if you wouldn't buy a copy of her religious paper then she
attacked with her handbag.)  they are much like bags of holding though
often seem to have things in them that you don't remember putting
there...

Women can of course get into men's clothes quite easily... perhaps even
be disguised as men (once a shop keeper (real life) refused to sell me
stockings because she thought I was a lad - perhaps she thought I was
going to rob a bank....).

What advantages do men have with clothes? Perhaps the sensitive nose
of the woman won't let her put on used clothes until they've had time 
to air... (perhaps this is becoming an argument for an attribute of sense
of smell rather than making it purely gender related...) 

Words

Women apparently tend to have a greater facility with languages (not me!)
perhaps reading spellbooks would be easier for them. And writing scrolls.

Chemicals

Men seem to me keener on chemistry (I found it boring - I only just
managed to scrape an A-level in it...and I was the only female in the
A-level chemistry class...) perhaps they could identify potions more
easily... maybe for male characters certain colour potions will always
turn out to be the same things...

Gossip

It seems to me that both sexes are jolly adept at this - but nethack's
shopkeepers are surprisingly unforthcoming...


